.TH SEMVER-FORGE 1 "2026-10-23" "semver-forge 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
semver-forge \- semantic version calculation and local Git release management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B semver-forge
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ command-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B semver-forge
calculates Semantic Versioning 2.0.0 versions from Conventional Commit history, validates and synchronizes configured version metadata, generates release notes, runs configured checks, and creates local annotated Git tags. It is designed to be reusable across repositories and does not require a remote hosting provider.
.PP
A command being available does not imply that a release is published. The release workflow is local-only and never pushes tags or publishes artifacts remotely.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --help ,\ -h
Show command help.
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed program version.
.TP
.BI --project \ DIR
Use the specified project directory. By default, the current directory is used to discover the Git repository.
.TP
.B --json
Emit JSON output for commands that support structured output.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create a starter .semver-forge.toml and create VERSION only if it does not already exist. Existing configuration is not overwritten.
.TP
.B doctor
Inspect Python, Git, repository state, configuration, and the configured version source.
.TP
.B current
Display the canonical version and its source.
.TP
.B validate VERSION
Validate a SemVer version string.
.TP
.B compare VERSION_A VERSION_B
Compare versions by SemVer precedence. Build metadata does not affect precedence.
.TP
.B bump patch|minor|major
Calculate an increment. Files are changed only when --write is supplied; --dry-run previews synchronization.
.TP
.B next [--explain]
Calculate the next version from commits since the latest recognized release tag or configured baseline.
.TP
.B sync [--version VERSION] [--dry-run]
Synchronize configured version sources. Without --dry-run, this changes configured files.
.TP
.B status
Summarize working-tree state, current version, latest release tag, and proposed next version.
.TP
.B history
Show commits since the release boundary.
.TP
.B check
Check agreement between the canonical version and configured synchronization targets.
.TP
.B changelog [--dry-run]
Generate release notes from the proposed release range.
.TP
.B release [patch|minor|major] [options]
Prepare and create a local release. Options include --version VERSION, --prerelease alpha|beta|rc, --dry-run, --notes-only, --build, and --yes. A real release requires a clean working tree by default. Dry-run and notes-only modes do not run tests/builds or modify files.
.TP
.B verify-tag
Verify the latest recognized release tag.
.TP
.B verify-release
Verify the latest release tag and whether it points to HEAD.
.TP
.B install [--prefix DIR]
Install the source-tree package into a prefix, defaulting to ~/.local.
.TP
.B uninstall [--prefix DIR]
Remove recognized Semver Forge installation files under the selected prefix.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
semver-forge --help
semver-forge init
semver-forge doctor --json
semver-forge validate 1.2.3-rc.1
semver-forge compare 1.2.3 1.3.0
semver-forge next --explain
semver-forge release --dry-run
semver-forge release patch --yes
semver-forge verify-release
.fi
.SH SAFETY
Release execution is intended for a clean Git working tree. Existing release tags must not be moved or overwritten. The tool does not push or publish releases remotely. Review project configuration and the dry-run plan before authorizing a real release. Configured hooks and build/test commands may execute code and must be reviewed before use.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .semver-forge.toml
Per-project configuration.
.TP
.I VERSION
The default canonical version source; projects may configure another source.
.TP
.I CHANGELOG.md
Optional generated changelog, depending on project configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR python3 (1)
.PP
Project documentation: README.md and docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Remote publishing and automatic push are not implemented. TOML writes and YAML parsing are not bundled in the current version-source adapters. See project documentation for current adapter and recovery limitations.
